# aitm — AI Tool Manager

A CLI to manage AI tool configurations (rules, steering files, skills, agents) from GitLab repositories. It fetches files from remote repos and installs them into the correct directories for your AI assistants. Which assistants are active is controlled by a global configuration (`~/.aitm/config.json`), so the same manifest works across different developer setups.

## Installation

### 1. Configure the npm registry

Add the following to your `~/.npmrc`:

```
@dx:registry=https://source.tui/api/v4/packages/npm/
//source.tui/api/v4/packages/npm/:_authToken=<YOUR_GITLAB_TOKEN>
```

### 2. Install globally

```bash
npm install -g @dx/aitm
```

## Configuration

Before using `aitm`, configure your GitLab access:

```bash
aitm config set-host https://source.tui
aitm config set-token <your-token>
aitm config set-assistants q kiro
aitm config show
```

Configuration is stored in `~/.aitm/config.json`.

---

## Interactive Mode (TUI)

When running in a terminal (TTY detected), aitm automatically enters interactive mode with arrow-key navigation, searchable lists, and guided prompts. This activates when required arguments are omitted:

```bash
aitm add              # Interactive: browse/search/manual file selection
aitm add file         # Interactive: prompts for repo, file, targets
aitm remove           # Interactive: select from manifest tools
aitm search           # Interactive: prompts for query, then offers to add results
aitm extend           # Interactive: browse/search/manual manifest selection
aitm config setup     # Interactive: guided wizard with arrow-key selection
aitm config set-env   # Interactive: prompts for key/value
aitm list files       # Interactive: prompts for repo, browse with search
```

To disable interactive mode (e.g. in scripts or CI):

```bash
aitm --no-interactive add file   # Errors if required args missing
```

When all required arguments and flags are provided, commands run immediately without prompts, even in a TTY.

