## Command Reference

### `aitm init`

Initialize a new `aitools.json` manifest in the current directory. If `aitools.json` already exists, the command exits with an error.

```bash
aitm init
```

---

### `aitm list`

List remote files from a GitLab repository. Requires a subcommand.

#### `aitm list files <repo>`

List available AI tool files (`.md` and `.json`) in a remote GitLab repository. Fetches the full repository tree and displays matching files.

```bash
aitm list files group/project
aitm list files group/project --path rules/
aitm list files group/project --limit 20
```

| Option | Description |
|---|---|
| `--path <subPath>` | Filter results to files under the given subdirectory path |
| `--limit <n>` | Maximum number of file results to display (default: unlimited) |

---

### `aitm add`

Add a tool to the `aitools.json` manifest. Requires a subcommand.

#### `aitm add file <repo> <filePath>`

Add a single file from a remote GitLab repository as a tool in the manifest. The file will be installed to the directories determined by the specified target(s).

You can also use `@N` to reference a result from the last `aitm search`:

```bash
aitm add file group/project path/to/file.md --target steering
aitm add file group/project path/to/file.md --target steering --target rule
aitm add file group/project path/to/file.md --target skill --name my-skill --description "Helpful guidance"
aitm add file group/project path/to/file.md --target rule --ref v1.0.0
aitm add file group/project path/to/file.md --target skill --alias custom-name
aitm add file @1 --target rule          # add search result #1
aitm add file @3 --target skill         # add search result #3
```

| Option | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--target <target...>` | Yes | Target type(s). Valid values: `rule`, `skill`, `steering`, `agent`, `default-agent`, `resource`. May be specified multiple times. |
| `--name <name>` | No | Skill name written as YAML frontmatter in the installed `SKILL.md`. Only applies to `skill` targets. |
| `--description <desc>` | No | Skill description written as YAML frontmatter in the installed `SKILL.md`. Only applies to `skill` targets. |
| `--resource-name <name>` | No | Resource name used as the install directory under `.kiro/`. Required for `resource` targets. Must be a valid folder name (alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores). |
| `--alias <alias>` | No | Override the install path segment (file/folder name under the target directory). May contain `/` for nested paths. |
| `--ref <ref>` | No | Pin to a specific Git ref (branch, tag, or commit SHA) instead of resolving HEAD at install time. |
| `--required-env <name:desc...>` | No | Required environment variable(s) in `name:description` format. May be specified multiple times. During install, aitm verifies these are set in `config.environment`. |
| `--manifest <name>` | No | Target a secondary manifest file (`<name>.aitools.json`) instead of `aitools.json`. Creates the file if it doesn't exist. |

**Valid targets and install directories:**

At install time, each target type is expanded into concrete assistant-specific installs based on the `assistants` configured in `~/.aitm/config.json`. The mapping is:

| Type | Assistant | Installs to |
|---|---|---|
| `rule` | q | `.amazonq/rules/aitm/` |
| `skill` | kiro | `.kiro/skills/aitm/` |
| `steering` | kiro | `.kiro/steering/aitm/` |
| `agent` | kiro | `.kiro/agents/aitm/` |
| `default-agent` | kiro | `.kiro/agents/aitm/` (also sets `chat.defaultAgent` in `.kiro/settings/cli.json`) |
| `resource` | kiro | `.kiro/<resource_name>/` |

If an assistant is not in the global config, its targets are silently skipped. An empty `assistants` list means all assistants are active.

**`default-agent` behavior:** Installs the agent file identically to `agent`, then reads the `name` property from the installed JSON file and writes it to `.kiro/settings/cli.json` as `chat.defaultAgent`. This makes the installed agent the default agent in Kiro. If the agent file is not valid JSON or lacks a `name` property, the settings update is skipped and the file installation still succeeds.

**Skill install behavior:** Single-file `skill` dependencies are installed as skill folders containing a `SKILL.md` file. For example:

```
.kiro/skills/aitm/
  custom-name/
    SKILL.md
```

If `--name` or `--description` is provided, the installed `SKILL.md` starts with YAML frontmatter:

```markdown
---
name: my-skill
description: Helpful guidance
---
# Original file content...
```

Without `--alias`, the folder name is derived from the original filename (minus extension). Folder dependencies are installed as-is and are not affected by the skill folder transformation.

**`resource` behavior:** Installs the file or folder into `.kiro/<resource_name>/`, where `<resource_name>` is specified via `--resource-name`. The resource name must be a valid folder name (alphanumeric characters, hyphens, and underscores only). Both single files and directories are supported. Example:

```bash
aitm add file group/project path/to/config.json --target resource --resource-name my-config
```

This installs the file to `.kiro/my-config/path/to/config.json`.

