## Manifest Schema

### `aitools.json` structure

```json
{
  "extends": [
    { "repository": "group/base-config" },
    { "repository": "group/team-config", "ref": "v1.0.0", "file": "custom.json" }
  ],
  "tools": {
    "<toolId>": {
      "repository": "group/project",
      "file": "path/to/file.md",
      "targets": [{ "type": "rule" }],
      "ref": "v1.0.0",
      "alias": "custom-name",
      "name": "skill-name",
      "description": "skill description",
      "required_environment_variables": [
        { "name": "MY_TOKEN", "description": "Token for API access" }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

### `extends` array

Each entry in the `extends` array references a remote manifest whose tools are merged into the local manifest during install.

| Field | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `repository` | Yes | GitLab project path of the remote repository |
| `ref` | No | Git ref (branch, tag, or SHA) to pin to. Defaults to HEAD. |
| `file` | No | Path to the manifest file in the remote repository. Defaults to `aitools.json`. |

### `tools` object

Each key is a tool identifier and each value describes where to fetch the file and where to install it.

| Field | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `repository` | Yes | GitLab project path |
| `file` | Yes | File path in the repository |
| `targets` | Yes | Array of `{ type }` objects |
| `ref` | No | Pinned Git ref |
| `alias` | No | Override install path segment |
| `name` | No | Skill name (skill targets only) |
| `description` | No | Skill description (skill targets only) |
| `required_environment_variables` | No | Array of `{ name, description }` objects. During install, aitm verifies these are set in `config.environment` before downloading any tools. |

### Validation rules

- `extends` entries must have a `repository` field

## How it works

- `aitools.json` — the manifest listing your tools and extends references
- `aitools-lock.json` — lock file pinning resolved SHAs for reproducible installs
- Files are fetched from GitLab at the pinned ref (or default branch HEAD) and placed in the appropriate assistant directory
- Extended manifests are resolved depth-first and merged, with local tools taking precedence

